        "id": "ch6_5_3-1",
        "text": "Interaction patterns\nThe success of a CWD-based system heavily depends on well-defined interaction patterns between\nagents. In an LLM-based implementation, these patterns must account for the unique characteristics\nof language model interactions. Essential interaction patterns include the following:\n\u2022 Message passing protocols :\nI Structured formats for agent-to-agent communication\nI Clear handoff procedures between different processing stages\nI Error handling and recovery mechanisms\n\u2022 State management :\nI How agents maintain awareness of their current task status\nI Methods for tracking progress through multi-step processes\nI Coordination of parallel activities\nSummary\n157\n\u2022 Feedback loops :\nI How agents communicate success/failure\nI Methods for requesting clarification or additional information\nI Mechanisms for continuous improvement through interaction history",
